---
import LegalPage from '../../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import KakuOwner from '../../../components/legal/KakuOwner.astro';
import { KAKU_DELETION_TERM, KAKU_MIN_AGE, LEGAL_EMAIL, SPAIN_DIGITAL_CONSENT_AGE } from '../../../lib/legal';
import { route } from '../../../i18n';
---
<LegalPage
  lang="en"
  routeKey="kakuPrivacy"
  title="Kaku! Privacy Policy | Kuxar Studio"
  heading="Kaku! Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy of the Kaku! app: what data is processed, on what legal basis, providers, retention periods, your rights and how to delete your account."
  updated="12 October 2026"
>
  <p>This policy explains how your personal data is processed when you use <strong>Kaku!</strong>, the app for learning to write Japanese. We wrote it to be understood: if anything is unclear, write to us.</p>

  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <KakuOwner lang="en" />

  <h2>2. What data we process, why and on what legal basis</h2>
  <table class="legal-table" tabindex="0">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis (GDPR)</th><th>Retention</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>User identifier generated by Firebase. If you sign in with Google: your Google account email, name and photo.</td>
        <td>Create your account (anonymous or Google), sync your progress across devices and show your profile in Settings.</td>
        <td>Performance of a contract: the app's terms of use (Art. 6(1)(b)).</td>
        <td>While you keep the account.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Progress: completed characters, practice counts, daily challenge results and streak.</td>
        <td>Save your progress and show your statistics.</td>
        <td>Performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b)).</td>
        <td>While you keep the account. You can reset it at any time from Settings.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>User identifier, purchase history and status (product, dates, refunds) and technical data to validate the purchase (IP address, device model and OS, app version).</td>
        <td>Verify the Sensei Pass purchase, unlock paid content, restore it if you change phones and remove it if the purchase is refunded.</td>
        <td>Performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b)) and legal obligations for handling refunds (Art. 6(1)(c)).</td>
        <td>While you keep the account and afterwards as required by legal obligations.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Pseudonymised usage statistics: lessons started and completed, stroke errors, use of the daily challenge and purchase screen, app instance identifier.</td>
        <td>Understand which parts of the app work and improve the content.</td>
        <td><strong>Your consent</strong> (Art. 6(1)(a)). Only collected if you accept.</td>
        <td>The retention period configured in Google Analytics (14 months at most).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Crash reports: stack trace, device model and OS, app version.</td>
        <td>Detect and fix bugs.</td>
        <td><strong>Your consent</strong> (Art. 6(1)(a)). Only sent if you accept.</td>
        <td>90 days (Firebase Crashlytics).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Device and app integrity signal (Firebase App Check with Play Integrity).</td>
        <td>Check that requests come from the genuine app and protect your data from abuse.</td>
        <td>Legitimate interest in the security of the service (Art. 6(1)(f)).</td>
        <td>Not stored: it is validated on each request.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Text of the suggestions you send us, your user identifier, date and app version.</td>
        <td>Read and act on your suggestions.</td>
        <td>Legitimate interest in handling the message you choose to send us (Art. 6(1)(f)).</td>
        <td>Up to 2 years, or until you delete your account.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>User identifier and date of the deletion request.</td>
        <td>Complete the deletion of your account with the providers the app cannot delete from on its own.</td>
        <td>Legal obligation to honour your right to erasure (Art. 6(1)(c)).</td>
        <td>Until the deletion is complete ({KAKU_DELETION_TERM.en} at most).</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Kaku! does not use advertising or the device's advertising ID, does not sell your data and does not build profiles that affect you. App settings (theme, language, sound, your choice about statistics) are stored only on your phone.</p>

  <h2>3. Statistics and crash reports: your choice</h2>
  <p>The first time you open the app we ask whether you accept usage statistics and crash reports. Nothing is collected until you answer. You can change your choice at any time in <strong>Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; legal</strong>, with a switch for each. Withdrawing consent does not affect processing carried out before.</p>

  <h2>4. Purchases (Sensei Pass)</h2>
  <p>Purchases are made through Google Play. Kaku! never receives or stores your card or payment details.</p>
  <p>To verify purchases we use <strong>RevenueCat</strong> (RevenueCat, Inc.), which acts as a processor on our behalf and receives the data in the purchases row of the table above. You can read its policy at <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" rel="noopener">revenuecat.com/privacy</a>.</p>

  <h2>5. Providers (processors)</h2>
  <p>We only share data with providers that process it on our behalf under a data processing agreement:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Ireland Limited / Google LLC</strong> (Firebase Authentication, Cloud Firestore, Google Analytics for Firebase, Firebase Crashlytics, Firebase App Check and Google Sign-In).</li>
    <li><strong>RevenueCat, Inc.</strong> (purchase verification and management).</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Google Play</strong> (Google) processes payments as an independent controller, under its own terms and privacy policy.</p>

  <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
  <p>Google and RevenueCat may process data in the United States. These transfers rely on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework where the company is certified and, in any case, on the European Commission's standard contractual clauses included in their data processing agreements (Art. 46 GDPR).</p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can exercise your rights of <strong>access, rectification, erasure, objection, restriction of processing and portability</strong> at any time, and withdraw your consent, by writing to <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_EMAIL}</a>. Include your user identifier or your Google account email so we can find your data. We reply within one month.</p>
  <p>If you believe we have not handled your request properly, you can lodge a complaint with the <strong>Spanish Data Protection Agency</strong> (<a href="https://www.aepd.es" rel="noopener">aepd.es</a>) or with the authority of your country of residence.</p>

  <h2>8. Deleting your account and data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>From the app:</strong> Settings &gt; Data management &gt; <strong>Delete account and data</strong>. Your account, progress, daily challenges and streak are deleted immediately. What the app cannot delete on its own (your RevenueCat record and the suggestions you sent) we delete within {KAKU_DELETION_TERM.en}.</li>
    <li><strong>Without the app:</strong> email <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_EMAIL}</a> from your account's email address, or see the <a href={route('kakuDelete', 'en')}>account deletion page</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Progress only:</strong> Settings &gt; Data management &gt; Reset progress. Your account and purchases are kept.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Google keeps the Google Play order record for its own legal and tax obligations.</p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>Kaku! is intended for users aged {KAKU_MIN_AGE} and over. In Spain, if you are under {SPAIN_DIGITAL_CONSENT_AGE} you need permission from a parent or guardian to sign in with Google, make purchases and accept statistics. If you are a parent or guardian and believe a child has given us data without your permission, write to us and we will delete it.</p>

  <h2>10. Security</h2>
  <p>All communications are encrypted (HTTPS). Database rules prevent one account from reading or changing another account's data, and nobody can unlock paid content from the app: that is decided by purchase verification. Firebase App Check blocks requests that do not come from the genuine app. If a security breach affecting your data occurred, we would notify the Spanish Data Protection Agency within 72 hours and, if it posed a high risk to you, we would also notify you.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy, we will update the date above. If the change is significant (for example, a new use of your data), we will notify you in the app before it applies.</p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>For any privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_EMAIL}</a>. See also the <a href={route('kakuTerms', 'en')}>Kaku! terms of use</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
